# ARK Shop Identity Doctrine

Full doc: `docs/platform/shop-identity-v1.md`

## Constitution

**HTTP is part of the product. SIP is part of the infrastructure. Provisioning is the translator between them.**

## Application

- `SHOP_BASE_URL` — authority for all **HTTP** capabilities (`/voice/*`, microbrowser, webhooks).
- `ShopBaseUrl` — derive product URLs only.
- Never `VOICE_HOST`, `VOICE_RUNTIME_HOST`, or `COMMUNICATIONS_VOICE_*` in PHP product code.

## Deployment transport (provisioning only)

- `VOICE_SIP_REGISTRAR`, `VOICE_SIP_PORT` — read via `VoiceTransportConfiguration`.
- **Do not derive SIP registrar from `SHOP_BASE_URL`.**
- `VOICE_HOSTNAME` — Coolify/Traefik/Asterisk stack only; never operator UI.

## Provisioning

Operator adds device → ARK generates config → provisioning reads transport config + shop HTTP URLs → device learns registrar and microbrowser. Operator never types transport.

## Reject

- Shared `voice.arksms.com` SIP edge without per-shop VPS routing
- SIP registrar in operator UI
- Coupling SIP hostname to product URLs in application code

## Deployment model

One shop → one VPS → one Asterisk. Scale by provisioning shops, not centralizing runtimes.
